; ============================================================================
; BASIC FUNCTIONS OF BANK 6
; BASIC functions of bank 6 (token-table bank byte 00H with handler 80D8H..8114H; EVFUNC
; calls them with the argument(s) on the evaluator stack, POPARG / ARGxxx fetch them,
; the result goes to XX / the string buffer):
;   INP(port), PEEK(addr), PEEK#(bank,addr), POINT(x,y) / POINT(n) (graphic dot / text
;   pattern), CHR$, HEX$, INSTR, ASC (2-byte codes -> 16-bit value), ERN, ERL, RXD$ (one
;   received COM byte, "?" on error, "" if none).
;   The kanji functions JS$, KN$, KLEN, KLEFT$, KMID$, KRIGHT$, ACNV$, KCNV$ point to a
;   bare RET (KJSNOP ACA7H / KNOTSUP AD2EH): the argument is passed through unchanged.
; Errors: 0FH string too long, 11H type, 12H argument, 13H range.
; ============================================================================

;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; AAA9H - Basic function RXD$
; One received COM byte; "?" on error, "" if none.
;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
